# Intergrax — Iteration Instruction (Harness AI)

Implement the **Intergrax Harness AI / Agent Operating System**. Full rules: **`AGENTS.md`** (hard constraints). This file adds workflow, **context budget**, and communication only.

## Strategic frame

- **Harness is the product** — agents are replaceable; runtime is permanent.
- Default scope: **gate maintenance** in `docs/plan/PLATFORM_FOUNDATION.md` §6.1 (hub only; satellites on demand under `docs/plan/plan/`).
- **Phase K** and **§6.3** require explicit operator reprioritization — never start silently.

## Context budget (mandatory — every session)

**Quality = targeted evidence, not bulk loading.**

- **One domain pair per session** unless the operator explicitly batches.
- Read **only** the selected `docs/architecture/<DOMAIN>.md` + scoped sections of `docs/plan/<DOMAIN>.md` (see below).
- **Never** load full plan files >500 lines — grep/open **§6**, open gap registers, and rows cited by the task only. Skip `(closed)`, `(complete)`, `Archived` unless re-validating a listed gap.
- **Never** re-read the same file in one session unless it changed.
- Prefer **grep with path filters** over repo-wide semantic search for known symbols.
- Run **only** verification commands relevant to the current item (`AGENTS.md` §Verification).
- Do **not** load `docs/audit_results/` unless RESUME/bootstrap says so.
- Respect **`.cursorignore`** — excluded paths are out of scope unless the operator points to them.

## Documentation model

```text
docs/intergrax_runtime_architecture.md  ← hub (pair picker)
docs/architecture/<DOMAIN>.md             ← canon
docs/plan/<DOMAIN>.md                   ← plan (scoped reads)
docs/guides/SYSTEM_INVARIANTS.md        ← skim cross-domain rules
```

22 paired domains — basename routing table in **`AGENTS.md` §Task routing**. Do **not** load unrelated pairs.

**Per iteration:** hub → invariants (skim) → architecture → **scoped** plan → implement smallest plan item → update both pair files if contracts change.

## Scope & work order

- **One coherent item**, one domain, unless operator requests a batch.
- Out-of-scope findings: report only — do not fix silently.
- Cycle: ANALYSIS → ARCH REVIEW → PLAN REVIEW → (IMPROVEMENT PROPOSAL) → DOCS → IMPLEMENT → VERIFY → CONCLUSIONS.
- **Safety fuse:** plan ↔ architecture ↔ ideal conflict → **STOP**, explain, propose doc fix before code.

## Architecture (never violate)

```text
Tier-0 intergrax/  ·  Tier-1 intergrax/runtime/  ·  Tier-2 agents/  ·  Tier-3 applications/

intergrax/ ↛ agents/|applications/   agents/ ↛ applications/   applications/ → agents/ + intergrax/
```

**Always:** strengthen Harness; reuse Tier-0; smallest coherent diff; Python 3.12 + `uv`; copyright on new files.  
**Never:** Tier-0 duplication; business logic in Nexus; agent-specific Nexus branches; vendor SDK in Tier-2; `getattr`/reflection where typed contracts exist; secrets in repo; whole-platform-complete claims; new docs without justification.

**New component gate:** existing mechanisms insufficient → STOP, explain alternatives, wait for operator.

**Mode I (idea audit):** operator triggers (`audyt pomysłu`, `idea audit`, …) → read **`.cursor/rules/intergrax-idea-audit.mdc`** — no code until approved.

## Language

| Context | Language |
|---------|----------|
| Repository artifacts | English |
| Operator chat (summaries, conflicts, reports) | Primary language of the session |

## Definition of Done

Follow **`AGENTS.md`**: verification bundle, ADR rules, iteration summary template, journal rule (`.cursor/rules/intergrax-implementation-journal.mdc`). Do not mark complete without tests evidence. **Do not commit** unless the operator asks.
